Project's main objective is to build a gene expression data resource where we can compare gene expression levels between genes and between biosamples. With the standard ARCHS4 dataset this is not possible, as the data are not normalized for transcript length and read depth.

In this folder, the clean up, categorization, filtration, and log transformation/normalization are done for the data to be usable. 

The files inside "refining/sbatch_files/makefiles" folder are the main files which:
1. Assign biosamples to biosample-categories
2. Filter biosamples based on a minimum required read depth (5K)
3. Gene length correction 
    * This also has a separate part where we had to convert and match ARCHS4 genes to a file containing transcript length per gene       inside "refining/gene_length_correction"
    
    * From the gene ENSMBL id, there were 7 genes: HERC3 (2), LINC03021 (2), LINC03023 (2), LINC03025 (2), MKKS (2), NPEPPSP1 (2),
      TNFRSF10A-DT (2) as seen in "refining/data_slash_results/archs4_TLF_geneLengthData.csv" where the the gene id matched to 
      same gene symbol name. For example, both ENSG00000254319 and ENSG00000277526 found in the TLF (transcript-length-file) 
      match to LINC03021. TLF, as a result, provides two different lengths for that gene: 3384 and 1714. We took the average 
      of the two values and divided the ARCHS4 value by that determined gene length value
      ("archs4_TLF_geneLengthData_averagedRepeats_LW20230416.csv"). Thus, that's why this first mentioned csv file has stores 
      57455 gene elements while in ARCH4 hdf5 has 57447 gene elements. 
    
4. Quantile normalization 

Run each of the corresponding ".sh" files in order with the ARCHS4 data. 
(*These files may need to be modified if ARCHS4 data's gene names are different from the v2.1 or continue to not have ENSEMBLE ID.)

############# ARCHS4 HDF5 File Contents #############
 
root = "/home/lwu/work/NarrativeGenomics/region_narration/code/pipeline/ARCHS4_LW/"
file_path = "refining/data_slash_results/"
filename = root + file_path + 'archs4_gene_human_v2.1_normalized_LW20230126.h5'

Groups: 
1. "data" 
    - "raw_matrix"
      The raw (but filtered and catgorized) ARCHS4 v2.1 data
      
    - "threshold_matrix"
      The 5M read count threshold filteration 
      
    - "corrected_matrix"
      Correcting for transcript-length 
      
    - "qn_matrix"
      Performed quantile normalization 
      
    - "highest_tier_category_matrix_raw" 
    - "lowest_tier_category_matrix_raw"
      Raw samples averaged across highest level tier and lowest level tier categories.
    
    - "highest_tier_category_matrix_qn"
    - "lowest_tier_category_matrix_qn"
      Raw samples averaged across highest level tier and lowest level tier categories.
    
    - "high_tier_oe_matrix_raw"
    - "low_tier_oe_matrix_raw"  
      Raw O/E Matrix for highest level and lowest level tier categories.

    - "high_tier_log2oe_matrix_raw"
    - "low_tier_log2oe_matrix_raw"
      Raw log2(O/E) Matrix for highest level and lowest level tier categories.
    
    - "high_tier_oe_matrix_qn"
    - "low_tier_oe_matrix_qn"  
      QN O/E Matrix for highest level and lowest level tier categories.

    - "high_tier_log2oe_matrix_qn"
    - "low_tier_log2oe_matrix_qn"
      QN log2(O/E) Matrix for highest level and lowest level tier categories.
   
     
2. "meta"
i. "biosamples"
    
    - "all_biosample_names"
      Raw matrix - all biosample names
      
    - "threshold_biosample_names"
      After 5M read count threshold filteration - all biosample names 
    
    - "category"
      After 5M filter, sample associated category 
    
ii. "genes"

    - "all_gene_names"
       All gene names 
       
    - "gene_description"
       Short gene description from gProfiler 
       
    - "gene_id"
      Gene ENSMB ID
      
    - "gene_length"
      Gene transcript length 

